📄 GreenFi Whitepaper 
Title: GreenFi – Decentralized Finance for Agricultural Forecasting
________________________________________
1. Abstract
GreenFi is a decentralized finance platform built on BlockDAG, designed to empower agricultural communities with prediction markets, staking, lending, and token swaps. It uses BDAG as its native token to deliver fast, secure, and transparent financial tools for farmers, traders, NGOs, and governments.
________________________________________
2. Problem Statement
Agriculture faces volatility from climate change, market instability, and limited access to financial tools. Smallholders lack affordable risk management, and institutions need decentralized food security data.
________________________________________
3. Solution
GreenFi offers a community-driven DeFi ecosystem that enables:
•	Binary prediction markets for agricultural forecasts
•	Staking BDAG for rewards and governance
•	Lending stablecoins against BDAG collateral
•	Token swaps via decentralized exchange (DEX)
•	Multi-chain deployment with sub-2 second transaction finality
________________________________________
4. Architecture
GreenFi’s architecture includes:
•	Smart contracts: PredictionMarket, Staking, Lending, DEX
•	Frontend: React + Ethers.js
•	Backend: Node.js + Express (optional)
•	Oracles: Chainlink + weather/crop APIs
•	Governance: DAO-ready staking-based voting
________________________________________
5. Tokenomics
GreenFi uses BDAG as its native utility and governance token:
•	No new token introduced
•	BDAG powers staking, lending, market creation, and voting
•	Incentives: staking rewards, liquidity mining, market resolution fees
•	Burn mechanism reduces BDAG supply over time
________________________________________
6. Use Cases
•	Farmers: Forecast yields, hedge risks, access loans
•	Traders: Analyze market sentiment, earn yield
•	NGOs/Governments: Monitor decentralized food security data
•	Investors: Gain exposure to agriculture via DeFi
________________________________________
7. Roadmap
GreenFi’s development is structured into six strategic waves:
🌱 Wave 1: Ideation & Scaffolds
•	Define GreenFi’s mission and stakeholders
•	Create smart contract scaffolds and frontend structure
•	Set up GitHub repository and publish initial README
🧪 Wave 2: Prototype & Architecture
•	Build demo of prediction markets using BDAG
•	Integrate mock weather/crop APIs
•	Design modular contracts and expand frontend
•	Update GitHub with architecture diagrams
🚜 Wave 3: MVP Deployment & Field Testing
•	Deploy MVP on BlockDAG testnet
•	Enable BDAG staking, market resolution, and claiming
•	Conduct field testing with farmers and cooperatives
•	Document feedback in README and whitepaper
🌾 Wave 4: Usability & Oracle Integration
•	Refine UI/UX for mobile and low-bandwidth users
•	Integrate Chainlink and custom oracles
•	Add lending and DEX modules
•	Document oracle logic and prepare for mainnet
🧱 Wave 5: DAO Governance & Documentation
•	Launch staking-based governance system
•	Finalize audits and security reviews
•	Write comprehensive documentation
•	Prepare GitHub and whitepaper for public release
🌍 Wave 6: Final Demo & Global Impact
•	Deliver final demo of full DeFi suite
•	Present GreenFi’s agricultural impact
•	Launch mobile app and multilingual support
•	Begin DAO-led expansion into new regions
________________________________________
8. Governance
GreenFi will evolve into a DAO where BDAG holders vote on:
•	Protocol upgrades
•	Treasury allocations
•	Market categories and resolution rules
Voting power is proportional to staked BDAG.
________________________________________
9. Security
GreenFi prioritizes security through:
•	Smart contract audits
•	Bug bounty programs
•	Upgrade-safe architecture
•	Transparent resolution logic and payout mechanisms
________________________________________
10. Conclusion
GreenFi aims to transform agriculture through decentralized finance, empowering communities with tools to forecast, hedge, and grow. By leveraging BDAG and blockchain technology, GreenFi delivers scalable, transparent, and inclusive financial infrastructure for global food systems.
